      "path": "site/index.html",
      "anchor": "<div data-hdb-input-precision=\"input-precision-20261023\">",
      "block": "<div data-hdb-coupled-mean-pilot=\"coupled-mean-pilot-20261025\"><p><strong>25 October 2026: a coupled five-mean response approximation passes its accuracy target.</strong> One continuously defined C1 approximation now includes the first coupled bulk feedback and shell boundary lift. Its complete conditional error bound is below 1.6090323e28 in the retained scaled X norm, meeting the 1e29 target. The 64 and 128 meshes gave insufficient bounds; the declared 256 limit passed. Both execution modes agree, and an independent exact integrator reproduces the stored feedback samples.</p><p>This advances the numerical construction of five mean coefficients. The full angular second-order spacetime, intrinsic observable sign, nonlinear family and physical origin remain unestablished. These are mathematical bounds under the stated model assumptions, not physical measurements. No new Zenodo version or journal submission accompanies this checkpoint.</p><p><a href=\"https://github.com/maldonado-research/HDblast/blob/main/research/HDBLAST_COUPLED_MEAN_PILOT_20261025/DERIVATION.md\">Derivation and scope</a> · <a href=\"https://github.com/maldonado-research/HDblast/tree/main/research/HDBLAST_COUPLED_MEAN_PILOT_20261025\">Frozen data, source and replay</a> · <a href=\"https://github.com/maldonado-research/HDblast/raw/refs/heads/main/research/HDBLAST_COUPLED_MEAN_PILOT_20261025.zip\">Source archive (ZIP)</a></p></div>\n\n",
